# Telemetry credentials, used by RELEASE builds only.
#
# The release workflow bakes these in at build time. A local build reads this
# file (dotenv is loaded only under debug_assertions) but never sends analytics
# with it — see QUILTSYNC_TELEMETRY_DEV below.
SENTRY_DSN=https://your-dsn-here@sentry.io/project-id
MIXPANEL_PROJECT_TOKEN=your-mixpanel-project-token-here
MIXPANEL_API_SECRET=your-mixpanel-api-secret-here

# Opt a local build in to telemetry. Unset (or 0) means none, which is what a
# developer who does nothing gets. Any other value opts in.
#
#   just start-telemetry
#
# Analytics then runs as a DRY RUN: every event is rendered to its exact wire
# form — the same name and properties a release would send — and written to the
# terminal. No client is constructed and nothing leaves the machine, so this
# needs no credentials and cannot reach a real project even if the token above
# is filled in. That is what makes it safe to leave real values here.
#
# The crash reporter has no dry run: the SDK either holds a client or it does
# not. So a local build reports crashes only if SENTRY_DSN is set, and then
# tagged environment=development. If you do not have a spare Sentry project,
# leave SENTRY_DSN empty and crash-side behaviour stays release-verified.
#
# Caveat: option_env! reads the *compiler's* environment, so credentials
# exported in the shell you build from are baked into your binary. Keep real
# values in this file, not in your shell profile.
QUILTSYNC_TELEMETRY_DEV=1
